{
 "idea": {
  "id": "overnight_index",
  "family": "overnight",
  "title": "Own the index only from the close to the next open",
  "why": "For decades nearly all of the US market's gain came overnight and almost none between the open and the close (Cooper, Cliff, Gulen 2008; Lou, Polk, Skouras 2019). If that still holds, owning the index fund only overnight earns the market's return with far less time at risk. It trades twice a day, every day, so even a one basis point cost each way is five percent a year.",
  "source": "Cooper, Cliff, Gulen 2008",
  "market": "us",
